## Context

Reopens [[0140-split-build-by-workpackage]] which was attempted on
2026-05-01 and abandoned after the worktree's commits drifted three weeks
behind a moving `Makefile`. The closing rationale: handoff-artifact
snapshots from the original work conflict with main's regenerated
versions, and `experiments/Makefile` has since grown new targets
(`exp1-reasoning-topup`, `exp1-cost-summary`, Pareto figure paths,
`p1_base.topup` extraction) that the original split did not consider.

The structural intent stands and matches the project rule in
`~/.claude/rules/coding-python.md`:

> Split the build by workpackage. Analysis (Python/R, data access) and
> writing (LaTeX, Quarto) workpackages live in separate Makefiles. A
> writing-side build must produce the manuscript from handoff artifacts
> alone — no `uv run`, no data fetch.

## Current state (2026-05-21)

The repository has two Makefiles:

- `experiments/Makefile` — analysis-side. Drives extract, evaluate,
  measurements.jsonl assembly, all tabulators (`tab_exp1_cost_summary`,
  `tab_exp1_reasoning_topup`, `tab_per_run`, etc.), all figures
  (`fig_census_direct`, `fig_pareto`, `fig_regimes_scatter`). Targets
  write into `../report/inputs/generated/` and `../slides/inputs/generated/`.
- No top-level / writing-side Makefile. `report/report.pdf` and
  `slides/slides.pdf` are built ad-hoc (manual tectonic / latexmk).

## Actions (v2)

1. Inventory the current `experiments/Makefile` (≈300 lines as of
   2026-05-21) and tag each target with its workpackage.
2. Create three Makefiles:
   - **`analysis.mk`** (or keep at `experiments/Makefile`) — everything
     that needs `uv run` / Python / network. Owns `measurements.jsonl`,
     all `.record.json` regeneration, all tabulators, all figures.
   - **`paper.mk`** at repo root — builds `report/report.pdf` from
     `report/inputs/generated/**` taken as committed inputs. TeX +
     bibtex only; no `uv run`.
   - **`slides.mk`** at repo root — builds `slides/slides.pdf` from
     `slides/inputs/generated/**` taken as committed inputs. TeX only;
     no `uv run`.
3. Top-level `Makefile` dispatches: `make analysis|paper|slides`
   delegate via `$(MAKE) -f <file>`.
4. Audit `report/inputs/generated/` and `slides/inputs/generated/` for
   completeness — every file `paper.mk`/`slides.mk` references must be
   committed. Add to `analysis.mk` any generator that's still missing.
5. Add `tests/test_makefile_split.py` (`@pytest.mark.adherence`)
   asserting `paper.mk`/`slides.mk` contain no `uv run`, no Python, no
   `wget`/`curl`.

## Test

Clean-room build of `paper.mk` and `slides.mk` in a container with
TeX Live only (no Python, no internet). Both must succeed from the
state of `report/inputs/generated/` and `slides/inputs/generated/` as
committed.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `analysis.mk`, `paper.mk`, `slides.mk` exist; top-level `Makefile`
      is dispatch-only.
- [ ] `paper.mk` and `slides.mk` build without Python / uv / network.
- [ ] Handoff manifest documented at the top of `analysis.mk`.
- [ ] Adherence test enforces "no Python in writing-side Makefiles".
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Differences from 0140

- Drop the original handoff-artifact-snapshot commit — regenerate
  fresh from current main's analysis pipeline.
- Account for new targets added since 2026-05-01: `exp1-reasoning-topup`,
  `exp1-cost-summary`, Pareto figure (`fig_pareto`), `p1_base.topup`
  extraction.
- Account for two new generated tables (`tab_exp1_cost_summary.tex`,
  `tab_exp1_reasoning_topup.tex`).
